  The second: integrate by parts ($u=\arcsin h$, $dv=h(1-h^2)^2dh$, $v=-\tfrac16(1-h^2)^3$); boundary terms vanish, giving $\tfrac16\int_0^1(1-h^2)^{5/2}dh=\tfrac16\cdot\frac{5\pi}{32}=\frac{5\pi}{192}$.
  The third is $M_3=\tfrac16$. Thus
